          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is L14-30 or 14-50 better for home backup?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "L14-30 is enough for most homes running a well pump and essential circuits, and it is the most common transfer switch connection. A 14-50 carries more current and suits generators above about 9,000 running watts powering central air or several big 240V loads. Match the outlet to your inlet and transfer switch rating."
